minimalBettiNumbers -- compute the minimal Betti numbers of a given graded ideal
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        minimalBettiNumbers(I, LengthLimit => lim)
  * Inputs:
      * I, a graded ideal of an exterior algebra
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * LengthLimit => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        infinity, only compute enough to determine the Betti table up to and
        including the column labelled lim
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,, the Betti table of the
        ideal I computed using its minimal generators

Description
===========

Example:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E=QQ[e_1..e_4,SkewCommutative=>true]                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = E                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
